>> title: Miso Soup
>> category: Soups
>> tags: miso, tofu, japanese, quick
>> servings: 4
>> time: 25 min
>> step.1: steep 10 min
>> step.2: steep 2 min, strain
>> step.3: warm 2 min
>> step.4: whisk in off the heat

Steep @kombu{1%piece}(4 in) in @water{4%cups}(950 mL) over low heat until it just begins to simmer, ~{10%min}, then lift out the kombu.

Steep @&(~1)broth{} off the heat for ~{2%min} with @katsuobushi{1%cup}(loosely packed), then strain it.

Warm @&(~1)dashi{} for ~{2%min} with @silken tofu{7%oz}(200 g; cubed) and @dried wakame{1%Tbs}.

Whisk @white miso{4%Tbs}(70 g) into @&(~1)dashi{} off the heat, without letting it boil.

Scatter @scallions{2}(thinly sliced) over @&(~1)soup{}.
